From: Kajcsi <64730213+Kajcsi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:09:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] vk_scheduler: pause, don't reset, the occlusion counter
 at each submission

EndPendingOperations runs before every Vulkan submission and reset the
ZPassPixelCount64 counter there (since Eden b1f3b568fb). A guest that resets
the counter, draws, and reports expects the report to cover every draw since
its own reset. When a submission lands between those draws and the report,
the reset drops the samples counted so far and the report reads too low.

The split GPU thread batches fence and command-list submissions on the back
thread (EDEN_NX2_FENCE_FLUSH_US), and other threads can force a pending flush
at any ring entry, so submissions now land mid-sequence often. In Ocarina of
Time (0400486024DEC000) this shows as one-frame white flashes on Link.

Pause the counter instead, as yuzu did, and keep the query running across
the submission. EndRenderPass already pauses it at render pass end, the next
draw resumes it, and the guest's own reset still clears it.

Tested in Kokiri Forest (RTX 4090, Low GPU accuracy, split=2), 36 s of
consecutive frames with Link on screen, same binary with a temporary switch:
old reset 15 and 9 flashes, this change 0 and 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

(cherry picked from commit e3cf9394c1891e8e44da584af7816c9ce06fcffb)
(cherry picked from commit e44ee5c79f15484e72e1ecf1b017302e8655d006)
---
 src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
index 15a474f66b..f2a5185dd3 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
@@ -524,7 +524,9 @@ void Scheduler::InvalidateState() {
 }
 
 void Scheduler::EndPendingOperations() {
-    query_cache->CounterReset(VideoCommon::QueryType::ZPassPixelCount64);
+    // Pause, don't reset: a submission can land between a guest's counter reset and its report,
+    // and resetting here would drop the samples counted so far (the report then reads too low).
+    query_cache->CounterClose(VideoCommon::QueryType::ZPassPixelCount64);
     EndRenderPass();
 }
 
